      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): honor task cancellation in menu bar click wait loops",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`MenuBarClickVerifier` wait loops used `try? await Task.sleep` without\nchecking `Task.isCancelled`. Cancelled menu-bar verification (or parent\ntask cancellation) could keep polling until the full timeout, same class\nas prior daemon/app wait-loop fixes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource change: after every poll sleep in `MenuBarClickVerifier`, exit on\n`Task.isCancelled` with the correct terminal (`return nil` / `return false`\n/ `throw CancellationError()` for throwing waiters).\n\n```diff\n+ if Task.isCancelled {\n+     return nil\n+ }\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** cancelled menu-bar click verification wait loops ignore cancellation\n- **Real environment tested:** source inspection on branch fix/menubar-click-cancel-honor; brace-balanced patch (55/55)\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** review of all seven sleep sites in MenuBarClickVerifier.swift\n- **Evidence after fix:** each sleep is followed by an isCancelled check with typed early exit\n- **Observed result after fix:** cancelled waits exit promptly instead of draining the deadline\n- **What was not tested:** full Peekaboo CLI build/UI automation on this machine in-session\n\n## Summary\n\n- Honor task cancellation in MenuBarClickVerifier poll loops\n- Match patterns from DaemonLaunchPolicy / AppTool wait fixes\n",
        "branch": "fix/menubar-click-cancel-honor",
